Visionary: Claude · Mode: audit continuation · For the Integrator to attack (you already audited these seams and returned APPROVED on feasibility — this plan binds them to rocks).

## Goal
Top management sees real sourcing KPIs at a glance; every accepted meeting becomes a structured, learnable win record; hiring needs originating in Databricks flow into the same intake→sourcing loop — all real data, zero synthetic, keys encrypted.

## Non-goals
Billing, mobile (Owner). Email open-tracking infrastructure (open rate shown as "not yet measured" until a tracking decision — no fake numbers). Databricks MCP (agent-conversational access) — Statement Execution API only this wave. Wave-3 refinements parked: durable server-side email-reply ingestion, server-loaded campaign objects for sourcing-agent, LinkedIn manual-send server ledger row.

## Verified seams (from your audit + 3-agent research — attack any that look wrong)
- WINLOG: single choke point createBookingFor commit (store.ts:3471-3496); all 5 booking call paths flow through it; in scope: candidate (sourcePlatform, matchScore, outreachHistory[{channel,at,...}], replyHistory), campaign, booking, full HermesState. touchCount = outreachHistory.length; winningChannel = last outreach entry channel; timeToBookMs = booking.createdAt − earliest outreach at; triggering reply intent from prev.replies. No server bookings table — HermesState JSONB persists wins for free. Existing learning layer: SkillUpdate + learnedParamsFor (skills.ts:182-251) takes aggregate signals — the WinRecord feeds it structured data. Weekly-report "winning patterns" are illustrative strings (mock-ai.ts:1440) — NOT truth; do not reuse.
- DASHBOARD: extend src/lib/metrics.ts (globalKpis :155-192, computeCampaignMetrics :94-138) with per-platform/per-campaign funnels from candidates.sourcePlatform × outreach channel × ledger status × bookings. New read-only /exec page reusing existing UI patterns (mission-control HUD derivations, TrendSpark, trust-page tiles). Open rate: NOT measurable today (no email-open events; only WhatsApp has receipt events via 0010 migration) — render as "not tracked yet", never a fake number.
- KPI TRUTH (prerequisite): 'contacted' is inconsistent — metrics.ts counts candidate stage high-water; HUD counts ledger status==='sent'. ONE canonical definition (ledger/outreach send facts) in metrics.ts, consumed by both.
- DATABRICKS (verified docs.databricks.com): POST {host}/api/2.0/sql/statements, Bearer auth; OAuth M2M service principal (POST {host}/oidc/v1/token, client_credentials, scope=all-apis, ~1h token, cache ~55min) or PAT for dev; parameterized statement (:since, TIMESTAMP) — never string-interpolate; wait_timeout='30s', on_wait_timeout='CONTINUE', disposition=INLINE, format=JSON_ARRAY (≤25MiB), row_limit guard; poll GET /api/2.0/sql/statements/{id} if PENDING; map manifest.schema.columns onto data_array (values arrive stringified). Keys via encrypted api_keys ("Databricks" provider, same pattern as Tavily/Apollo). Rows map into the intake shape → createCampaignFromAnalysis (the same path a pasted email takes).

## Standards (unchanged from Wave 1 + these)
Zero synthetic data in exec metrics — provenance-filter demo candidates out of live KPIs or label demo mode loudly. Honest gaps ("not tracked yet") over invented numbers. All secrets encrypted (DATA_ENCRYPTION_KEY set). Gate stays green. Reduced-motion + responsive on /exec.

## Rocks (build order)
- **Rock W1 — KPI truth**: canonical metric definitions in metrics.ts, REAL-FACT based: contacted = distinct candidates with a REAL COMPLETED send fact — OutreachMessage.dryRun === false AND sentAt != null (or a provider/server-ledger terminal status:'sent'; manual LinkedIn confirm at store.ts:2660-2685 and provider-send transitions at store.ts:2813-2821 are the counting points). NOT ledger status:'sent' alone (demo dry-run writes those, store.ts:2537-2585) and NOT dryRun:false alone (live approval sets dryRun:false with sentAt:null while ledger is only 'claimed' — approved≠sent). Live KPIs additionally exclude candidate.provenance === 'synthetic'. replyRate/positiveRate/booked similarly fact-based. Consumed by globalKpis, campaign metrics, AND the HUD (one source). Proof: `npx tsx tests/metrics-canonical.mts` with a fixture including THREE trap cases — (a) demo dry-run 'sent' (dryRun:true), (b) live approved-unsent (dryRun:false, sentAt:null, ledger 'claimed'), (c) synthetic candidate — asserting ALL THREE are excluded, plus HUD/metrics agreement.
- **Rock W2 — WinRecord + winlog** (consumes W1's real-fact model): `wins: WinRecord[]` on HermesState appended atomically in createBookingFor's commit ({candidateId, name, campaignId, bookingId, at, sourcePlatform, leadSource, matchScore, seniority, role title, outreachChannel, touchCount (real COMPLETED sends per W1: dryRun:false AND sentAt!=null), timeToBookMs, triggeringReplyIntent, messageTraits via explicit join candidate.outreachHistory[].messageId → state.outreach}). BOUNDED: cap wins at 500 newest (FIFO trim in the same commit) to protect the JSONB doc. Export: PRIVATE, authenticated in-app view + download ONLY (candidate PII — never written to docs/, public/, _relay/, .rocket-fuel/, never committed). Wins feed learnedParamsFor as structured signals (skills.ts). Proof: `npx tsx tests/winlog.mts` — drive a booking on fixture state incl. dry-run touches, assert structured win with correct REAL touchCount/channel/timing + cap behavior; export path is in-app only (grep assert no docs/public write).
- **Rock W3 — /exec dashboard**: read-only exec page: KPI tiles (sourced, contacted, reply rate, positive-reply rate, meetings booked, time-to-source, avg match score), per-platform funnel, per-campaign funnel, trend sparklines, wins feed (from W2), open-rate tile labeled "not tracked yet". RBAC: viewer may see aggregate, PII-redacted tiles only; admin required for export/config; page-session gated by proxy in live. Demo mode banners itself as synthetic and excludes nothing (it IS the demo); LIVE mode excludes provenance:'synthetic' AND dryRun:true from every tile (per W1). Proof: `npx tsx tests/exec-dashboard.mts` — fixture asserts synthetic+dryRun exclusion in live derivations, canonical-metrics agreement, no Math.random/hardcoded metric constants (grep assert), viewer-vs-admin gating, renders (login-page.mts style).
